shape theory.coherence.law2 : theory.coherence, theory.contact.self {
  type: law
  layer: 0
  """
// Law 2 (Conservation).
// In a coherent shape, structure cannot be created from nothing
// or destroyed into nothing.
//
// Self-contact carries character from M to M' through structure S.
// If M' contains content with no grounding in the prior character,
// the transformation produced something from nothing: the self-contact
// shape's output does not follow from its input through its structure.
// The transformation is ill-defined at that step.
//
// If content in the prior character vanishes without trace, subsequent
// self-contact references what no longer exists.
//
// Conservation follows from self-contact alone: what crosses the
// contact boundary must derive from what was there. What exists after
// must come from what existed before.
//
// Conservation does not preclude transformation. Content can change
// form while maintaining continuity.
//
// Derives from: theory.coherence, theory.contact.self
  """
}
